<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ecore:EPackage xmi:version="2.0" xmlns:xmi="http://www.omg.org/XMI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xmlns:ecore="http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore" name="test" nsURI="test" nsPrefix="test">
  <eAnnotations source="Version">
    <details key="value" value="1.0"/>
  </eAnnotations>
  <eAnnotations source="http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/GenModel">
    <details key="complianceLevel" value="17.0"/>
    <details key="oSGiCompatible" value="true"/>
    <details key="basePackage" value="org.eclipse.fennec.codec.v2.example"/>
    <details key="resource" value="XMI"/>
  </eAnnotations>
  <eClassifiers xsi:type="ecore:EClass" name="ExampleSingleID">
    <eAnnotations source="http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/GenModel">
      <details key="documentation" value="myId is automatically treaten as ID field per default (ID_FIELD) the Json looks like this:&#xA;&#xA;'''&#xA;{&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_id&quot;: &quot;john&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;test&quot;: &quot;whatever ...&quot;&#xA;}&#xA;```&#xA;with option BOTH&#xA;&#xA;'''&#xA;{&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_id&quot;: &quot;john&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;myId&quot;:&quot;john&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;test&quot;: &quot;whatever ...&quot;&#xA;}&#xA;```&#xA;&#xA;with option FEATURE_NAME:&#xA;&#xA;'''&#xA;{&#xA;&#x9;&quot;myId&quot;: &quot;john&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;test&quot;: &quot;whatever ...&quot;&#xA;}&#xA;```&#xA;"/>
    </eAnnotations>
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EAttribute" name="myId" eType="ecore:EDataType http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore#//EString"
        iD="true"/>
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EAttribute" name="test" eType="ecore:EDataType http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore#//EString"/>
  </eClassifiers>
  <eClassifiers xsi:type="ecore:EClass" name="ExampleMultipleIDs">
    <eAnnotations source="http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/GenModel">
      <details key="documentation" value="myId, mySecondId, myThirdId are automatically treaten as ID fields per default (ID_FIELD) the Json looks like this.&#xA;The point is that the genmodel complains about having more than one idField. the ecore validation in return, does not complain, when having more than one idField&#xA;&#xA;having the option or EAnnotation set: separator=&quot;-&quot;&#xA;&#xA;myId=John&#xA;mySecondId=Doe&#xA;myThirdId=1&#xA;&#xA;'''&#xA;{&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_type&quot;: &quot;...#//ExampleMulipleIDs&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_id&quot;: &quot;John-Doe-1&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;test&quot;: &quot;whatever ...&quot;&#xA;}&#xA;```&#xA;with option BOTH&#xA;&#xA;'''&#xA;{&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_type&quot;: &quot;...#//ExampleMulipleIDs&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_id&quot;: &quot;John-Doe-1&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;myId&quot;:&quot;John&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;test&quot;: &quot;whatever ...&quot;m&#xA;&#x9;&quot;mySecondId&quot;:&quot;Doe&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;myThird&quot;:&quot;1&quot;&#xA;}&#xA;```&#xA;&#xA;with option FEATURE_NAME, that would no makes sense?:&#xA;&#xA;'''&#xA;{&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_type&quot;: &quot;...#//ExampleMulipleIDs&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;myId&quot;:&quot;John&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;test&quot;: &quot;whatever ...&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;mySecondId&quot;:&quot;Doe&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;myThird&quot;:&quot;1&quot;&#xA;}&#xA;```&#xA;&#xA;in structured mode and ID_FIELD (like the first example) it could look like:&#xA;&#xA;'''&#xA;{&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_type&quot;: &quot;...#//ExampleMulipleIDs&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_id&quot;: {&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;separator&quot;:&quot;-&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;myId&quot;:&quot;John&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;mySecondId&quot;:&quot;Doe&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;myThirdId&quot;:&quot;1&quot;&#xA;&#x9;}&#xA;&#x9;&quot;test&quot;: &quot;whatever ...&quot;&#xA;}&#xA;```&#xA;&#xA;with BOTH otion and structured:&#xA;&#xA;'''&#xA;{&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_type&quot;: &quot;...#//ExampleMulipleIDs&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_id&quot;: {&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;separator&quot;:&quot;-&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;myId&quot;:&quot;John&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;mySecondId&quot;:&quot;Doe&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;myThirdId&quot;:&quot;1&quot;&#xA;&#x9;}&#xA;&#x9;&quot;myId&quot;:&quot;John&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;test&quot;: &quot;whatever ...&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;mySecondId&quot;:&quot;Doe&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;myThird&quot;:&quot;1&quot;&#xA;}&#xA;```&#xA;"/>
    </eAnnotations>
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EAttribute" name="myId" eType="ecore:EDataType http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore#//EString"
        iD="true"/>
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EAttribute" name="test" eType="ecore:EDataType http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore#//EString"/>
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EAttribute" name="mySecondId" eType="ecore:EDataType http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore#//EString"
        iD="true"/>
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EAttribute" name="myThirdId" eType="ecore:EDataType http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore#//EString"
        iD="true"/>
  </eClassifiers>
  <eClassifiers xsi:type="ecore:EClass" name="ExampleMultiple">
    <eAnnotations source="http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/GenModel">
      <details key="documentation" value="Instead of providing the separator and idFeatures information using the config builder we exemplary use the EAnnotations here.&#xA;We have no id field, but even if we should only consider EAttributes mentioned in the idFeatures EAnnotation. Because the EAttribuite firstName and lastName are &#xA;no ID Fields, they will be serialized anyway&#xA;&#xA;firstName=John&#xA;lastName=Doe&#xA;&#xA;'''&#xA;{&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_type&quot;: &quot;...#//ExampleMuliple&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_id&quot;: &quot;John.Doe&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;firstName&quot;:&quot;John&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;lastName&quot;:&quot;Doe&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;test&quot;: &quot;whatever ...&quot;&#xA;}&#xA;```&#xA;with option BOTH would eventually not make sense, because it would be the same like the default above?&#xA;with option FEATURE_NAME, that would no makes sense?&#xA;&#xA;In structured format it could look like this:&#xA;&#xA;'''&#xA;{&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_type&quot;: &quot;...#//ExampleMuliple&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_id&quot;: {&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;separator&quot;:&quot;.&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;firstName&quot;:&quot;John&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;lastName&quot;:&quot;Doe&quot;&#xA;&#x9;}&#xA;&#x9;&quot;firstName&quot;:&quot;John&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;lastName&quot;:&quot;Doe&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;test&quot;: &quot;whatever ...&quot;&#xA;}&#xA;```&#xA;"/>
    </eAnnotations>
    <eAnnotations source="http://eclipse.org/fennec/codec">
      <details key="separator" value="."/>
      <details key="idFeatures" value="firstName, lastName"/>
    </eAnnotations>
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EAttribute" name="test" eType="ecore:EDataType http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore#//EString"/>
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EAttribute" name="firstName" eType="ecore:EDataType http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore#//EString"/>
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EAttribute" name="lastName" eType="ecore:EDataType http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore#//EString"
        iD="true"/>
  </eClassifiers>
  <eClassifiers xsi:type="ecore:EClass" name="IdClass01">
    <eAnnotations source="http://eclipse.org/fennec/codec">
      <details key="separator" value="_"/>
      <details key="idFeatures" value="userGroup, userId"/>
    </eAnnotations>
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EAttribute" name="userId" lowerBound="1"
        eType="ecore:EDataType http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore#//ELong"/>
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EAttribute" name="userGroup" lowerBound="1"
        eType="ecore:EDataType http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore#//EString"/>
  </eClassifiers>
  <eClassifiers xsi:type="ecore:EClass" name="ExampleIDClass01">
    <eAnnotations source="http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/GenModel">
      <details key="documentation" value="Instead of providing the separator and idFeatures information using the config builder we examplary use the EAnnotations here.&#xA;We have no id field exist, but the idFeatures EAnnotation is set to a reference&#xA;&#xA;if an IdClass01 instance is set with:&#xA;userId=42&#xA;userGroup=sales&#xA;&#xA;'''&#xA;{&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_type&quot;: &quot;...#//ExampleIDClass01&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_id&quot;: &quot;sales_42&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;test&quot;: &quot;whatever ...&quot;&#xA;&#x9;&quot;myId&quot;:{&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;userId&quot;:42,&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;userGroup&quot;:&quot;sales&quot;&#xA;&#x9;}&#xA;}&#xA;```&#xA;with option BOTH would eventually not make sense, because it would be the same like the default above:&#xA;with option FEATURE_NAME, that would no makes sense?&#xA;&#xA;But in structured it could look like this (structured make only sense with multiple fields):&#xA;&#xA;'''&#xA;{&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_type&quot;: &quot;...#//ExampleIDClass01&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_id&quot;: {&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;separator&quot;:&quot;_&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;userGroup&quot;:&quot;sales&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;userId&quot;:42&#xA;&#x9;}&#xA;&#x9;&quot;test&quot;: &quot;whatever ...&quot;&#xA;&#x9;&quot;myId&quot;:{&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;_type&quot;:&quot;...#//IdClass01&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;userId&quot;:42,&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;userGroup&quot;:&quot;sales&quot;&#xA;&#x9;}&#xA;}&#xA;```"/>
    </eAnnotations>
    <eAnnotations source="http://eclipse.org/fennec/codec">
      <details key="idFeatures" value="myId"/>
    </eAnnotations>
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EAttribute" name="test" eType="ecore:EDataType http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore#//EString"/>
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EReference" name="myId" eType="#//IdClass01"
        containment="true"/>
  </eClassifiers>
  <eClassifiers xsi:type="ecore:EClass" name="ExampleIDClass02">
    <eAnnotations source="http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/GenModel">
      <details key="documentation" value="Instead of providing the separator and idFeatures information using the config builder we examplary use the EAnnotations here.&#xA;We have no id field exist, but the idFeatures EAnnotation is set to a reference. The containing class &quot;IdClass02&quot; has an id field.&#xA;&#xA;if an IdClass02 instance is set with:&#xA;userId=42&#xA;userGroup=sales&#xA;&#xA;'''&#xA;{&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_type&quot;: &quot;...#//ExampleIDClass02&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_id&quot;: &quot;42&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;test&quot;: &quot;whatever ...&quot;&#xA;&#x9;&quot;myId&quot;:{&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;userId&quot;:42,&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;userGroup&quot;:&quot;sales&quot;&#xA;&#x9;}&#xA;}&#xA;```&#xA;with option BOTH would eventually not make sense, because it would be the same like the default above:&#xA;with option FEATURE_NAME, that would no makes sense?&#xA;&#xA;But in structured it could look like this (structured make only sense with multiple fields):&#xA;&#xA;'''&#xA;{&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_type&quot;: &quot;...#//ExampleIDClass02&quot;,&#xA;&#x9;&quot;_id&quot;: {&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;userId&quot;:42&#xA;&#x9;}&#xA;&#x9;&quot;test&quot;: &quot;whatever ...&quot;&#xA;&#x9;&quot;myId&quot;:{&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;userId&quot;:42,&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&quot;userGroup&quot;:&quot;sales&quot;&#xA;&#x9;}&#xA;}&#xA;```"/>
    </eAnnotations>
    <eAnnotations source="http://eclipse.org/fennec/codec">
      <details key="idFeatures" value="myId"/>
    </eAnnotations>
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EAttribute" name="test" eType="ecore:EDataType http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore#//EString"/>
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EReference" name="myId" eType="#//IdClass02"
        containment="true"/>
  </eClassifiers>
  <eClassifiers xsi:type="ecore:EClass" name="IdClass02">
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EAttribute" name="userId" lowerBound="1"
        eType="ecore:EDataType http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore#//ELong" iD="true"/>
    <eStructuralFeatures xsi:type="ecore:EAttribute" name="userGroup" eType="ecore:EDataType http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/Ecore#//EString"/>
  </eClassifiers>
</ecore:EPackage>
